ole-authorized action = a coverage gap to close' and 'Andrew ruled ENUMERATE over bless-the-override'. The YANG_PIPELINE_DEPLOY, DATA_REFRESH_DEPLOY and PUBLIC_DATA_ROUTER_DEPLOY entries are the same shape; the last of those was grantor-landed BEFORE the commits so its record carried zero overrides. This one carries exactly one, and stops there. SCOPE HELD DELIBERATELY NARROW: 4.0.0_SA_CRO and its laptop tilde lanes only. NOT 1.0.0_SA_CTO -- it gave the arch input and explicitly did not ask for write access, and a grant nobody requested is a widening. NOT ~Y/~Z -- those are the Codex and site-Z conventions and this is a LAPTOP-placed directive (D14, Andrew-ruled). A CRO lane that appears later is REFUSED until enumerated, which is the correct failure direction for an allow-list. SoD: GRANTOR is 0.0.0_AB_MSTR, GRANTEE is 4.0.0_SA_CRO -- the grantee did not commit its own grant, on this file's own ANY_EXEC_OR_AE lane, exactly as the CRO_WORKSPACE and CVO_WORKSPACE precedents did. Added 2026-09-12 by 0.0.0_AB_MSTR on 4.0.0_SA_CRO~D request 96241, CTO arch input 96245, D14 minted ff4dfaf23e.); agent=1.0.0_SA_CTO not in permitted_agents;VIOLATION: infra/logic/06_CONFORMANCE_LEDGER.md -- lane=PLATFORM_LOGIC_DOCS (The D14 Platform Logic foundation folder (infra/logic/**) -- DOCUMENTS ONLY: a README, ORDER_OF_OPERATIONS, the estate census, the doctrine and the analysis that feed the pipeline canon. WHY A NARROWER ENTRY UNDER infra/ RATHER THAN A DIFFERENT HOME: Andrew named the path himself (2026-09-12 ~18:0xZ, VERBATIM 'Persist this group of artifacts in a folder in ajb_workspace/infra/logic'), and a seat re-siting a folder he named in order to dodge a lane would be solving the gate's problem by editing his sentence. THE LANE RULE'S REASON DOES NOT REACH IT: infra/** is CLOUD_OPS_OR_ETL because in this estate infra/ has meant DEPLOYABLE infrastructure -- Terraform, Lambda source, EC2 -- and an AE owns what gets applied to the account. infra/logic/ holds no Terraform, no La